Conclusion - Ethical reflection and Improvements
The evolution of gaming platforms has continued to improve the accessibility and convenience of video games throughout the years with great success, but as new technology emerges ethical concerns and issues will continue to arise especially around topics relating to consumer rights and reliability of online services. It should be game companies responsibility to make sure that consumer protection is balanced with continuing to create new technology and to be considerate of what might happen in the long run for certain video games or consoles.

conclusion - second viewpoint analysis
Overall, how we play games has changed how we hang out and build friendships. It went from loud arcades at the mall with your friends to sitting on the couch, and then to talking through headsets with people online. Now with cloud gaming and games like Fortnite acting as virtual hangouts, almost anyone can jump in from anywhere. It's way easier to stay in touch now, even if interactions feel a bit less personal or face to face than they used to. At the end of the day, gaming still brings people together, just in digital spaces instead of real ones.